# retroforge-gpu-priority — an implicit Vulkan layer that runs a game's queues at LOW global
# priority, so the shell (OpenGamepadUI), Xwayland and mangoapp preempt the game's GPU work instead
# of queueing behind its frames. The source is ours to carry (no upstream tarball): patches/0001
# adds it as new files into the empty directory the PKGBUILD's prepare() makes, which is how a
# repo-owned source rides this pipeline and gets hashed by packages/inputhash.sh like any other
# patch.
#
# Enabled per game by RETROFORGE_GAME_LOWPRIO=1, which usr/bin/retroforge-launch puts in each
# emulator's environment. See the PKGBUILD and the patch header for the mechanism.
name: retroforge-gpu-priority
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
patches: 0001-add-the-game-priority-layer.patch
